From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] pam_group: membership from the group database without Open Directory

pam_group asks mbr_check_membership(3), which Libinfo answers through
opendirectoryd. NeoDarwin's Libinfo is built without it (DS_AVAILABLE off,
docs/base/libsystem.md) and answers EIO, so no one was ever a member and
su(1)'s "group=admin,wheel ruser root_only" check refused everyone. When the
call fails, check the group database as the module's FreeBSD code does: the
user's primary group, or the group's member list (Libinfo's file module:
/etc/group).

--- a/modules/pam_group/pam_group.c
+++ b/modules/pam_group/pam_group.c
@@ -122,8 +122,21 @@
 			continue;
 		if (mbr_gid_to_uuid(grp->gr_gid, g_uuid) != 0)
 			continue;
-		if (mbr_check_membership(u_uuid, g_uuid, &ismember) != 0)
+		if (mbr_check_membership(u_uuid, g_uuid, &ismember) != 0) {
+			/*
+			 * NeoDarwin: no directory service answers (Libinfo
+			 * without Open Directory: EIO). The group database
+			 * does, as on FreeBSD: the primary group, or a member.
+			 */
+			char *const *list;
+
+			if (pwd->pw_gid == grp->gr_gid)
+				goto found;
+			for (list = grp->gr_mem; *list != NULL; ++list)
+				if (strcmp(*list, pwd->pw_name) == 0)
+					goto found;
 			continue;
+		}
 		if (ismember)
 			goto found;
 	}
